  "question": {
    "text": "A wire of length <math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>,</mo></math> is made by joining two wires <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> of same length but different radii <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> and <math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> and made of the same material. It is vibrating at a frequency such that the joint of the two wires forms a node. If the number of antinodes in wire <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math> and that in <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></math> then ratio <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></math> is:<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0106_98c7cd336f64.png\" />"
